<title>SRI LANKA: Kelani Valley up on retail buying.</title>
<headline>Kelani Valley up on retail buying.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kelani Valley Plantations Ltd rose 4.3 percent, or one rupee, to 24.25, on retail buying of 5,000 shares, brokers said.</p>
<p>&quot;Small retail investors are keen on plantation shares since tea prices are up,&quot; said a local broker specialising in retail trade.</p>
<p>&quot;The shares are also cheap, but not so liquid anymore which means the slightest interest drives up price,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>Kelani Valley is one of six privatised plantation firms trading in Colombo.</p>
<p>--Colombo newsroom (941) 434319</p>
</text>
